<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan gold prices seen subdued on low demand.</title>
<headline>Pakistan gold prices seen subdued on low demand.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan gold prices are likely to remain subdued amid low demand this week, dealers at the Karachi bullion market said on Monday.</p>
<p>Gold was being traded in a narrow range as jewellers reported low sales, one dealer said. Silver prices were expected to remain stable, he added.</p>
<p>							 Saturday   April 16</p>
<p>    Gold 24 carat in rupees per 10 grams   4,612	4,573</p>
<p>    Silver per 1,000 grammes		   6,687	6,687</p>
<p>($1 = 40.34 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
